IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2006 (NT) -- from the seat of THE PERSON WHO PAID FOR A VICTIM'S FUNERAL (Part 4,
-- Division 5A, funeral expense assistance). "Can I apply? Am I in time? How much can I get? When must I be paid? Must
-- I repay? Can I seek review? What can my lawyer charge?" Section 47B puts a duty-bearing position on this person (the
-- application, the refund in s 47G), and the Act applies to them as "the applicant" (s 4), so they get their own seat
-- beside the victim's (voca-seat.l4). Both seats draw on the same core (voca-core.l4), so they cannot disagree about the
-- law; every name here differs from the victim seat's.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Funeral expense assistance -- the questions of the person who paid for the funeral`

-- The person who died, as a primary victim (s 9), from plain answers. A death directly caused by a criminal act in the
-- Territory makes it a violent act under s 5(1)(b) whatever the offence, so the offence record is not read: its fields
-- are placeholders.
GIVEN `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they died as a direct result of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person who died was a primary victim killed by a violent act, from my funeral answers` `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` `they died as a direct result of the act` IF
        `is a primary victim` `the deceased`
    AND `they died as a direct result of the act`
    WHERE
        `the act` MEANS
            `Criminal act` WITH
                `occurred in the Territory`                                        IS `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory`
                `constitutes a criminal offence, or would but for an excuse in s 5(2)(b)` IS `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse`
                `directly resulted in the injury or death of one or more persons`  IS `they died as a direct result of the act`
                `the offence`                                                      IS `no offence details`
        -- placeholder offence: not read where the death itself makes the act a violent act (s 5(1)(b))
        `no offence details` MEANS
            `Offence` WITH
                `section`                                                        IS ""
                `was an attempt`                                                 IS FALSE
                `was committed before 25 March 2024`                             IS FALSE
                `was committed before 30 April 2023`                             IS FALSE
                `the victim suffered serious harm as a direct result`            IS FALSE
                `was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon` IS FALSE
                `was committed by a person in the company of another person`     IS FALSE
                `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(a) applied`                    IS FALSE
                `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(c) applied`                    IS FALSE
                `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(k) applied`                    IS FALSE
                `the condition opposite it in Schedule 2 applied`                IS FALSE
                `how many related criminal acts the violent act is a series of`  IS 1
                `the related acts occurred over a period of time`                IS FALSE
                `the acts were committed against the same victim by the same offender` IS FALSE
        `the deceased` MEANS
            `Person and the violent act` WITH
                `the act is a violent act`                                                   IS `is a violent act` `the act`
                `the act is a compensable violent act`                                       IS `is a compensable violent act` `the act`
                `the act was committed against the person`                                   IS `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest`
                `the person suffered an injury as a direct result`                           IS FALSE
                `the person died as a direct result`                                         IS `they died as a direct result of the act`
                `the person was injured or died trying to prevent the act, help or rescue a victim, or arrest the offender` IS `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest`
                -- placeholders: the categories other than primary victim are not read for a funeral
                `the person was present at the scene and was injured as a direct result of witnessing the act` IS FALSE
                `the person was injured as a direct result of later becoming aware of the act` IS FALSE
                `the person is a child or stepchild of the primary victim, or a child under their guardianship` IS FALSE
                `the person is a parent, step-parent or guardian of the primary victim`      IS FALSE
                `the primary victim was a child when the act occurred`                       IS FALSE
                `the person is the spouse or de facto partner of the primary victim`         IS FALSE
                `the person was entirely or substantially dependent on the primary victim for financial support` IS FALSE
                `the person is a relative of the primary victim, or in an intimate personal relationship with them` IS FALSE
                `the person committed the violent act`                                       IS FALSE

§§ `ss 47A-47E -- can I apply, am I in time, and how much`

@export Can I apply for funeral expense assistance for the funeral of someone killed by a violent act (ss 47A, 47B)?
GIVEN `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person died after a criminal act that happened in the Northern Territory
      `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, mental impairment, other incapacity or a lawful defence
      `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was committed against the person who died, or they died trying to prevent it, help or rescue someone, or arrest the offender
      `they died as a direct result of the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died as a direct result of the act
      `I have paid or will likely pay for the funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have incurred, or are reasonably likely to incur, the costs of their funeral
      `I committed the violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the violent act (then you cannot apply, s 47B(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` IF
    `is eligible to apply for funeral expense assistance` (`the person who died was a primary victim killed by a violent act, from my funeral answers` `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` `they died as a direct result of the act`) `I have paid or will likely pay for the funeral` `I committed the violent act`

@export Is my application for funeral expense assistance in time, within 2 years after the death (s 47C)?
GIVEN `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply (or will apply) to the Director
GIVETH A `Funeral time answer`
DECIDE `Is my funeral application in time` IS
    `the s 47C answer for` `the date of death` `the date I apply`

DECLARE `Funeral amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `none: I am not eligible to apply (s 47B)`
    `none: the application is late and the Director has not accepted it (ss 47C, 47E(2)(b))`

@export How much funeral expense assistance can I get: my reasonable funeral costs less what an insurer or other organisation paid, up to $15 000 for the funeral (ss 47B(4), 47C, 47D, 47E(2))?
GIVEN `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person died after a criminal act that happened in the Northern Territory
      `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse
      `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was committed against the person who died, or they died trying to prevent it, help, or arrest the offender
      `they died as a direct result of the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they died as a direct result of the act
      `I have paid or will likely pay for the funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have incurred, or are reasonably likely to incur, the funeral costs
      `I committed the violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the violent act
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply to the Director
      `the Director accepts my late application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you apply more than 2 years after the death: whether the Director accepts the late application because the circumstances justify it; otherwise no
      `the funeral costs the Director considers reasonable` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral costs you incurred or will incur that the Director considers reasonable, in Australian dollars
      `what an insurer or other organisation paid for the funeral` IS A NUMBER @desc Amounts paid by an organisation to you or for you for the funeral, including under an insurance policy (a funeral fund, a motor accidents or workers compensation funeral benefit), in Australian dollars
      `funeral expense assistance already paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc Funeral expense assistance already paid to you or for you for this funeral, in Australian dollars
      `funeral expense assistance already paid to others` IS A NUMBER @desc Funeral expense assistance already paid to anyone else for this funeral, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Funeral amount answer`
DECIDE `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` IS
    IF (NOT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` `the death followed a criminal act in the Northern Territory` `that act was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `the act was against the person who died, or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest` `they died as a direct result of the act` `I have paid or will likely pay for the funeral` `I committed the violent act`)
    THEN `none: I am not eligible to apply (s 47B)`
    ELSE IF     (`the s 47C answer for` `the date of death` `the date I apply`) EQUALS `late: the Director may accept it only if the Director considers the circumstances justify it (s 47C(2))`
            AND (NOT `the Director accepts my late application`)
         THEN `none: the application is late and the Director has not accepted it (ss 47C, 47E(2)(b))`
         ELSE `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` (`the most further funeral expense assistance` `the funeral costs the Director considers reasonable` `what an insurer or other organisation paid for the funeral` `funeral expense assistance already paid to me` `funeral expense assistance already paid to others`)

§§ `ss 47F-47G -- payment and refund (asked once the Director decides, or a refund is required)`

@export Within how many days after the Director decides to pay must the Territory pay my funeral expense assistance (s 47F)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must my funeral assistance be paid` IS
    `the days the Territory has to pay` `funeral expense assistance (s 47F)`

@export If the Director requires me to refund funeral expense assistance, how many days do I have after I receive the notice, before it is overdue as a debt to the Territory (s 47G)?
GIVEN `the days the refund notice gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Director's refund notice gives you, counted from when you receive it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How long do I have to refund funeral assistance` IS
    `the days to refund` `the days the refund notice gives me`

§§ `ss 47H-47K -- if CVSU could not contact me (asked only if a closure notice was sent)`

@export My funeral expense application was, or may be, closed because I could not be contacted: is it open, closed, or must it be reopened (ss 47H-47K)?
GIVEN `a closure notice was sent to me about my funeral application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a CVSU officer sent you a notice of proposed closure after failing to contact you for at least 3 months
      `I gave new contact details within 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a CVSU officer updated contact details within 30 days after the date of the notice
      `the date of the closure notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice of proposed closure
      `I asked for my funeral application to be reopened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the Director to reopen the closed application
      `the date I asked for reopening, or today` IS A DATE @desc The date you asked the Director to reopen it, or today's date if you have not
GIVETH A `Closure answer`
DECIDE `Is my funeral application open or closed` IS
    `the ss 47H-47K answer for` `a closure notice was sent to me about my funeral application` `I gave new contact details within 30 days` `the date of the closure notice` `I asked for my funeral application to be reopened` `the date I asked for reopening, or today`

§§ `s 48 and Schedule 1 -- review by NTCAT (asked once a decision is made)`

DECLARE `Funeral decision` IS ONE OF
    `the Director's decision on my application for funeral expense assistance`
    `the Director's decision requiring me to refund funeral expense assistance`

@export Can I apply to NTCAT for review of the Director's funeral expense decision (s 48, Schedule 1 items 4 and 5)?
GIVEN `the funeral decision` IS A `Funeral decision` @desc The decision: the Director's decision on your application for funeral expense assistance (s 47E), or requiring you to refund it (s 47G(1))
      `days since I was given the funeral decision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you were given the decision
      `days the NTCAT Act allows for review` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Northern Territory Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2014 allows to apply for review (not in the deposited texts: give the figure)
GIVETH A `Review answer`
DECIDE `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` IS
    `the s 48 answer for` `the decision` TRUE `days since I was given the funeral decision` `days the NTCAT Act allows for review`
    WHERE
        -- The person asking is the applicant (item 4) or the individual required to refund (item 5).
        `the decision` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the funeral decision`
            WHEN `the Director's decision on my application for funeral expense assistance` THEN `the Director's decision under s 47E on an application for funeral expense assistance`
            WHEN `the Director's decision requiring me to refund funeral expense assistance` THEN `the Director's decision under s 47G(1) requiring a refund of funeral expense assistance`

§§ `s 54 -- legal costs (asked only if a lawyer acts for me)`

@export What can my lawyer charge me for my funeral expense assistance application (s 54)?
GIVEN `the lawyer's reasonable disbursements` IS A NUMBER @desc The lawyer's reasonable disbursements (out-of-pocket expenses), in Australian dollars
      `counsel's fees in the disbursements` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those disbursements is counsel's (a barrister's) fees, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
DECIDE `What can my lawyer charge me for the funeral application` IS
    `the s 54 answer for` `an application for funeral expense assistance (Division 5A)` `the lawyer's reasonable disbursements` `counsel's fees in the disbursements`
